<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  body {
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: #000;
  }
  h1, h2, h3 {
    font-weight: bold;
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-top: 15px;
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }
  td {
    padding: 5px 0;
  }
  .section-header {
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-top: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
</style>
<body>
  <div class="page">
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
      <span style="font-size: 1.2em;">University of Rochester</span>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
      <p>Reporting Form for Financial Interests, Outside Activities and Scholarly Activities</p>
    </div>
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 20px;">
      <div>
        <p>Name:</p>
        <div style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; display: inline-block; min-width: 300px;">
          <span data-field="full_name">{{ full_name }}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Title:</p>
        <div style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; display: inline-block; min-width: 300px;">
          <span data-field="title">{{ title }}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 30px;">
      <div>
        <p>School/Department(s):</p>
        <div style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; display: inline-block; min-width: 300px;">
          <span data-field="school_department">{{ school_department }}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Period:</p>
        <div style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; display: inline-block; min-width: 300px;">
          <span data-field="reporting_period">{{ reporting_period }}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
      <p><strong>Due:</strong> March 1, 2026 (for annual reporting process)</p>
      <p><strong>Purpose:</strong> The purpose of this survey is to report all (1) Financial Interests that could directly and significant affect the design, conduct, or reporting of University research, and (2) Outside Activities and Scholarly Activities that interfere with or have the potential to interfere with an individual's ability to meet Institutional Responsibilities. The goal is to assist faculty members and others in identifying and managing potential conflicts of interest and conflicts of commitment in their University activities. By reporting and managing Financial Interests, Outside Activities, and Scholarly Activities, the University of Rochester and its faculty and staff can work together to avoid situations that may appear to compromise their integrity. Completion of this survey also fulfills federal grant requirements for reporting of financial interests in research.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header">Who Must Complete This Survey:</div>
    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
      <li>All University of Rochester faculty members with paid academic, clinical or research appointments;</li>
      <li>All study coordinators or other employees actively involved in negotiation or conduct of sponsored research, internally funded research that involves human subjects, or proposals for such funding;</li>
      <li>Other non-faculty members or Covered Individuals when required by the Faculty Policy on Conflict Commitment and Conflict of Interest in Research.</li>
    </ul>

    <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
      <p><strong>Timing:</strong> This survey must be completed within 60 days of appointment/hire, annually no later than March 1st for the prior year, and to provide updates after the annual reporting cycle has been completed (e.g. when a new financial interest is acquired that is related to a faculty member's research).</p>
      <p><strong>Appendix A</strong> includes key definitions included in this survey. For more background on the UR policy requirements, refer to the <a href="#">Faculty Policy on Conflict Commitment and Conflict of Interest in Research</a>. You may also contact your Dean, the <a href="#">Office of Research Integrity, Scholarship and Ethics (ORISE)</a> or Office of Counsel.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="page">
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 20px;">
      <p>Please answer the following questions:</p>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
      <p><strong>A. Did you participate in any Outside Activities (paid or unpaid)?</strong></p>
      <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <label><input type="radio" name="q_a_yes" value="yes"> Yes</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="q_a_no" value="no"> No</label>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 15px;">Do not include salary support from University of Rochester grants or contracts OR activities related to or income from seminars, lectures, or teaching engagements sponsored by a Federal, state, or local government agency, an Institution of higher education as defined at 20 U.S.C. 1001(a), an academic teaching hospital, a medical center, or a research institute that is affiliated with an Institution of higher education; or income from service on advisory committees or review panels for a Federal, state, or local government agency, an Institution of higher education as defined at 20 U.S.C. 1001(a), an academic teaching hospital, a medical center, or a research institute that is affiliated with an Institution of higher education.</p>
      <p style="margin-top: 15px;"><strong>Note:</strong> Receipt of payment or anything else of value from a foreign source must be reported.</p>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
      <p><strong>B. Did you participate in any Scholarly Activities that resulted in you receiving payment or anything else of value during the previous calendar year?</strong></p>
      <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <label><input type="radio" name="q_b_yes" value="yes"> Yes</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="q_b_no" value="no"> No</label>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 15px;">Do not include salary support from University of Rochester grants or contracts, OR activities related to or income from seminars, lectures, or teaching engagements sponsored by a Federal, state, or local government agency, an Institution of higher education as defined at 20 U.S.C. 1001(a), an academic teaching hospital, a medical center, or a research institute that is affiliated with an Institution of higher education.</p>
      <p style="margin-top: 15px;"><strong>Note:</strong> Receipt of payment or anything else of value from a foreign source must be reported.</p>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
      <p><strong>C. Do you or any of your family members (spouse, domestic partner, dependent children) have any intellectual property rights, e.g. patents, trademarks, copyrights, licenses, or royalties?</strong></p>
      <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <label><input type="radio" name="q_c_yes" value="yes"> Yes</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="q_c_no" value="no"> No</label>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 15px;">(Note: Do not include intellectual property rights that are owned by the University of Rochester.)</p>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
      <p><strong>D. Do you or any of your family members (spouse, domestic partner, dependent children) have any ownership, employment or fiduciary relationship with an outside organization that does business with, or seeks to do business with, the University?</strong></p>
      <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <label><input type="radio" name="q_d_yes" value="yes"> Yes</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="q_d_no" value="no"> No</label>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
      <p><strong>E. Do you or any of your family members (spouse, domestic partner, dependent children) own or control equity (e.g. stock or other ownership not held through a mutual fund) in any company with a business interest that is related to your Institutional Responsibilities (e.g. research, teaching, clinical or administrative duties)?</strong></p>
      <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <label><input type="radio" name="q_e_yes" value="yes"> Yes</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="q_e_no" value="no"> No</label>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
      <p><strong>F. Are you or any of your family members (spouse, domestic partner, dependent children) an officer, director, partner or employee in any company or organization with a business interest that is related to your Institutional Responsibilities (e.g. research, teaching, clinical or administrative duties)?</strong></p>
      <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <label><input type="radio" name="q_f_yes" value="yes"> Yes</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="q_f_no" value="no"> No</label>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
      <p><strong>G. Do you or any family members (spouse, domestic partner, dependent children) have any other activities outside of the University of Rochester, or received any other external payments or Financial Interests that could appear to be related to your University responsibilities, not already reported in the preceding survey questions?</strong></p>
      <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <label><input type="radio" name="q_g_yes" value="yes"> Yes</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="q_g_no" value="no"> No</label>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 15px;">If you answered Yes to any of the above questions, please explain your answers. Include a description of your activities, number of days (if applicable) you participated in the activity(ies), and amount of compensation or value. If you participate in UR research funded by an outside entity with which you have an interest as indicated above, or if your UR research involves a drug or device of the entity, describe the study and your role in the study.</p>
      <div style="border: 1px solid #000; height: 150px; margin-top: 10px; padding: 10px;">
        <span data-field="explanation_g">{{ explanation_g }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
      <p><strong>H. Are you involved in or have an application to either a “Foreign Talent Recruitment Program” or “Malign Foreign Talent Recruitment Program”?</strong></p>
      <p>Before answering this question, review the definitions of “Foreign Talent Recruitment Program” and “Malign Foreign Talent Recruitment Program” in the University’s <a href="#">Policy on Foreign Talent Recruitment Programs and Malign Foreign Talent Recruitment Programs</a> and the University’s <a href="#">guidance on these programs</a>. If you need assistance before answering this question, you can also contact the University’s Research Security Officer (Joe Doyle; <span data-field="security_officer_email">{{ security_officer_email }}</span>) for consultation.</p>
      <p style="margin-top: 15px;"><strong>Note:</strong> Participation in a Malign Foreign Talent Recruitment Program is prohibited for “Covered Individuals,” as defined in the <a href="#">Policy on Foreign Talent Recruitment Programs and Malign Foreign Talent Recruitment Programs</a>. Participation in a Foreign Talent Recruitment Program must be reported as Current and Pending (Other) Support and disclosed on the Biosketch to federal agencies, if applicable.</p>
      <div style="margin-top: 15px;">
        <label><input type="radio" name="q_h_yes" value="yes"> Yes</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="q_h_no" value="no"> No</label>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 15px;">If yes, attach any supporting documentation describing the program: (1) The name of the organization or program, (2) the nature of your responsibilities in the program, (3) the duration of your commitment (specifically either total number of days, weeks, or months, or give a date range), and (4) the amount of compensation you received during the reporting period and have received to date during the current calendar year as a result of participating in the program. Supporting documentation includes, but is not limited to, copies of contracts, grants, or other agreements (including appointment letters).</p>
      <div style="border: 1px solid #000; height: 150px; margin-top: 10px; padding: 10px;">
        <span data-field="explanation_h">{{ explanation_h }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
      <h3 style="text-align: center;">1. QUESTIONS ON EXTERNAL APPOINTMENTS, EXTERNAL POSITIONS, AND EXTERNAL FUNDING SUPPORT</h3>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="page">
    <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
      <p>Is your University research supported by active federal funding, or do you expect to apply for or receive federal funding for your University research during the upcoming year?</p>
      <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <label><input type="radio" name="q_federal_funding_yes" value="yes"> Yes</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="q_federal_funding_no" value="no"> No</label>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 15px;">If yes, please answer the following questions regarding external appointments, external positions, and external research support. Note: these relationships may need to be disclosed to funding sponsors to meet Federal requirements, and supporting documentation may need to be included with this survey. If you have any questions regarding disclosure in Current and Pending (Other) Support documents or Biosketches, contact your <a href="#">ORPA Research Administrator</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
      <p><strong>1. Do you hold a paid or unpaid scientific academic, professional, or institutional appointment, position or employment at any organization other than the University of Rochester? This includes unpaid appointments or positions such as guest, adjunct, honorary, or visitor titles.</strong></p>
      <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <label><input type="radio" name="q1_yes" value="yes"> Yes</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="q1_no" value="no"> No</label>
      </div>
      <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; margin-top: 15px;">
        <li>If yes, note that this appointment or position must be disclosed on your Biosketch submitted to federal agencies.</li>
        <li>If yes, identify whether this appointment, position, or employment is paid or unpaid.</li>
        <li>Paid <input type="checkbox" name="q1_paid" value="yes"> Unpaid <input type="checkbox" name="q1_unpaid" value="yes"></li>
        <li>If yes, describe the appointment, position, or employment and identify the institution, organization, or entity.</li>
      </ul>
      <div style="border: 1px solid #000; height: 100px; margin-top: 10px; padding: 10px;">
        <span data-field="description_q1">{{ description_q1 }}</span>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 15px;">If yes, is this appointment, position, or employment with a foreign institution, organization, or entity?</p>
      <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <label><input type="radio" name="q1_foreign_yes" value="yes"> Yes</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="q1_foreign_no" value="no"> No</label>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 15px;">If yes, attach any supporting documentation relating to the foreign appointment, position, or employment with this survey. Supporting documentation includes, but is not limited to, copies of contracts, grants, or other agreements (including appointment letters).</p>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
      <p><strong>2. Do you have any current or pending awards or contracts that support your research activities that are made through an external entity or made directly to you?</strong></p>
      <p><strong>Note:</strong> You are not required to report awards or contracts funded by or through the University, such as those awards or contracts made by federal funding agencies to the</p>
      <div style="border: 1px solid #000; height: 100px; margin-top: 10px; padding: 10px;">
        <span data-field="description_q2">{{ description_q2 }}</span>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 15px;">If yes, is any of the support provided by a foreign institution, organization, or entity?</p>
      <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <label><input type="radio" name="q2_foreign_yes" value="yes"> Yes</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="q2_foreign_no" value="no"> No</label>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 15px;">If yes, attach any supporting documentation relating to the support or resources with this survey. Supporting documentation includes, but is not limited to, copies of contracts, grants, or other agreements (including appointment letters).</p>
      <p style="margin-top: 15px;">If yes, specify which of the noted sources of support are from a foreign institution, organization, or entity.</p>
      <div style="border: 1px solid #000; height: 100px; margin-top: 10px; padding: 10px;">
        <span data-field="description_q2_foreign">{{ description_q2_foreign }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
      <p><strong>3. Are you hosting or planning to host any postdoctoral scholars, students, visiting scholars, or employees that are supported by an external entity?</strong></p>
      <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <label><input type="radio" name="q3_yes" value="yes"> Yes</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="q3_no" value="no"> No</label>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 15px;">If yes, note that this support must be reported as Current and Pending (Other) Support or as Facilities, Equipment & Other Resources to federal agencies.</p>
      <p style="margin-top: 15px;">If yes, describe and identify the external entity providing support.</p>
      <div style="border: 1px solid #000; height: 100px; margin-top: 10px; padding: 10px;">
        <span data-field="description_q3">{{ description_q3 }}</span>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 15px;">If yes, is any support provided by a foreign institution, organization, or entity?</p>
      <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <label><input type="radio" name="q3_foreign_yes" value="yes"> Yes</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="q3_foreign_no" value="no"> No</label>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="page">
    <div style="margin-top: 50px; margin-bottom: 50px;">
      <h3 style="text-align: center;">Certification:</h3>
      <p>I certify that (a) the responses above are true and complete to the best of my knowledge, (b) I have read the University of Rochester <a href="#">Faculty Policy on Conflict Commitment and Conflict of Interest in Research</a>, and (c) I am in compliance with University of Rochester policies related to conflicts of interest and commitment. I will comply with any conditions or restrictions imposed by the University to manage actual or potential conflicts of interest.</p>
      <p>Faculty who procure goods and services under Federal awards must complete the “2 CFR 200 Procurement Principles” training that is located in MyPath. This training is also required for all research staff and administrators who have been delegated the authority to purchase goods and services from Federal funds.</p>
      <p>I agree to notify my Dean or other immediate supervisor and update this form when my Financial Interests or Outside Activities significantly change.</p>
    </div>

    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 80px;">
      <div>
        <p>Name:</p>
        <div style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; display: inline-block; min-width: 300px;">
          <span data-field="signature_name">{{ signature_name }}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Date:</p>
        <div style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; display: inline-block; min-width: 300px;">
          <span data-field="signature_date">{{ signature_date }}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="page">
    <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
      <h3 style="text-align: center;">Appendix A</h3>
      <p><strong>“Outside Activity”</strong> means any activity or employment, paid or unpaid, performed outside the scope of a Faculty member’s Institutional Responsibilities for or on behalf of an entity that is not part of, the University, and that relates to a Faculty member’s Institutional Responsibilities. An Outside Activity includes, but is not limited to, outside employment, consulting, service on non-University corporate or advisory boards, participation in foreign talent recruitment programs, self-employment, participation in a business partnership, executive, management, or board positions with a not-for-profit entity, creation of business entities (for profit or not-for-profit), or academic appointments held outside of the University. Scholarly Activities are excluded from the definition of Outside Activities.</p>
      <p><strong>“Institutional Responsibilities”</strong> refers to a Faculty member’s professional responsibilities and obligations to the University associated with their University appointment, position, or employment, including those defined in applicable University policies, the University of Rochester Faculty Handbook, the SMD Regulations of the Faculty, faculty regulations or handbooks of applicable Schools or divisions, any agreement or document specifying the Faculty member’s relationship to the University, or applicable law, including responsibilities for research, teaching, clinical activities, administration, and institutional or internal committee service. Institutional Responsibilities also include those responsibilities assigned by the Dean, department chair, or other supervisor to the Faculty member within their department, center, or division.</p>
      <p><strong>“Scholarly Activity”</strong> means any scholarly activity consistent with the norms of scholarly practice in the Faculty member’s discipline. The following are examples of Scholarly Activities: (a) peer review of articles, book manuscripts, and grant or contract proposals; (b) speaking engagements at academic or research institutions or government agencies; (c) leadership positions in professional societies; (d) acting in an editorial capacity for a professional journal; (e) serving on a federal, state, or local government agency, committee, panel, or commission related to the Investigator’s area of scholarly activity; and (f) serving on, but not chairing, master’s or doctoral thesis committees at another university or academic institution. Any activity that would be considered a “Malign Foreign Talent Recruitment Program” or “Foreign Talent Recruitment Program,” as defined in the Malign Foreign Talent Recruitment Programs & Foreign Talent Recruitment Programs Policy, is excluded from the definition of Scholarly Activities.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>